    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2026 accelerated again, revenue up 17.8% to $331.8 billion on Microsoft Cloud growth, with Intelligent Cloud up 29.7% on Azure [F10][D472][P17][D916]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Microsoft Cloud reached $214.4 billion, 64.6% of revenue, and contributed 16.2pp of the 17.8% FY2026 growth [S24][D566][D568][D472]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Server products and cloud services revenue rose 31% to $129.4 billion, driven by Azure and other cloud services growing 41% [S61][P12]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Microsoft 365 Commercial products and cloud services added $14.2 billion, a 5.1pp contribution, on Copilot and E5 revenue per user [S64][D649][P14]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 20.8% against 17.8% revenue growth, an incremental margin of 53.3% [D473][D472][D498]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS grew 31.6% against 31.3% net income growth, with the share count down only 0.2% [D476][D474][D493]."}
